{"result":"{
  "id": "18559",
  "key": "SFCC-282",
  "summary": "Cart - Out of Stock and Partial Out of Stock",
  "customfield_10231": {
    "value": "*Full OOS* \n\n# Given an item in a Shopper's cart has become fully out of stock, when the cart renders, then an inline error message is displayed beneath the affected line item reading \"This item is unavailable\" in red.\n# Given an item in a Shopper's cart has become fully out of stock, when the cart renders, then a page-level error banner is displayed at the top of the cart drawer reading \"An item in your bag is unavailable\" with a red X icon\n# Given an item in a Shopper's cart has become fully out of stock, when the cart renders, then both the + and – stepper controls are disabled and visually greyed out on the affected line item — only Remove and Wishlist actions remain available.\n# Given an item in a Shopper's cart has become fully out of stock, when the cart renders, then an error message is displayed in the order summary reading \"Please remove unavailable item or save to wishlist to continue\" in red\n# Given an item in a Shopper's cart has become fully out of stock, when the Shopper views the button group, then the Checkout CTA, Apple Pay and Google Pay Express buttons remain visually enabled but are blocked at backend level from processing.\n# Given a Shopper removes the fully OOS item or moves it to wishlist, when the action completes, then all error states are cleared — the banner dismisses, the order summary error clears, and the Shopper can proceed to checkout via the Checkout CTA, Apple Pay, or Google Pay Express.\n# Given a cart contains multiple items and one becomes fully OOS, when the cart renders, then only the affected line item displays the inline error — all other items display normally.\n\n*Partial OOS (Limited Stock)*\n\n# Given an item in a Shopper's cart has limited stock and the quantity in the cart exceeds what is available, when the cart renders, then a page-level error banner is displayed at the top of the cart drawer reading \"An item in your bag has limited stock\" with a red X icon\n# Given an item in a Shopper's cart has limited stock and the quantity exceeds what is available, when the cart renders, then an inline error message is displayed beneath the affected line item reading \"Quantity unavailable in this size\" in red.\n# Given an item in a Shopper's cart has limited stock, when the cart renders, then the + stepper control is disabled and visually greyed out while the – control remains enabled so the Shopper can reduce their quantity to the available stock level.\n# Given an item in a Shopper's cart has limited stock, when the cart renders, then an error message is displayed in the order summary reading \"Please reduce item quantity to proceed\" in red\n# Given an item in a Shopper's cart has limited stock and the quantity exceeds what is available, when the Shopper views the Checkout CTA, then the Checkout CTA, Apple Pay and Google Pay Express buttons remain visually enabled but are blocked at backend level from processing.\n# Given a Shopper reduces the quantity of the affected line item to match or fall below the available stock level, when the quantity updates, then all error states are cleared — the banner dismisses, the inline error clears, the order summary error clears, and the Shopper can proceed to checkout via the Checkout CTA, Apple Pay, or Google Pay Express.\n\n*Error Messaging*\n\n# Given the cart contains an item that is fully or partially out of stock, when error messages are displayed (inline on the cart line item, in the page-level banner, and above the Checkout CTA in the order summary),then all error message copy must be driven by a configurable content source and must not be hardcoded in the codebase"
  }
}"}

